Fix two bugs in the PATH-scan (`zstyle ':completion-sync:path' enabled true`).

1. Ordering. find_fpaths_from_path walks $path front-to-back but prepends each
   hit, so the array comes out in reverse-PATH order; path_hook then iterates it
   {N..1} and prepends each entry to $fpath, inverting it again. Net effect: the
   last PATH entry wins. A nix devshell (front of PATH) therefore loses to the
   system profile, so a devshell's completion script gets paired with a
   different version of the binary it completes. Appending matches
   functions_from_xdg_data, which already returns XDG order for an identical
   {N..1} loop, and makes the "Prepend in reverse order" comments true. It also
   fixes the (u) dedup, which now keeps the first PATH occurrence, not the last.

2. Dead branch. The PATH-changed branch compares the dir list against a copy of
   itself, so it never fires -- the scan only ever ran once, at shell init, and
   entering a devshell mid-session added nothing at all. Re-scan before
   comparing.

Applies to 0.4.0 and 0.4.1. Upstream: BronzeDeer/zsh-completion-sync.

--- a/zsh-completion-sync.plugin.zsh
+++ b/zsh-completion-sync.plugin.zsh
@@ -87,6 +87,7 @@
       if [[ -d "$maybe_fpath" ]]; then
         _completion_sync:debug_log ':completion-sync:path:path2fpath' "found fpath on path: $maybe_fpath"
-        completion_sync_fpaths_from_path=("$maybe_fpath" $completion_sync_fpaths_from_path)
+        # Must stay in PATH order: callers iterate this backwards and prepend to $fpath
+        completion_sync_fpaths_from_path=($completion_sync_fpaths_from_path "$maybe_fpath")
       fi
     done
   done
@@ -347,6 +348,8 @@
     _completion_sync:debug_log ':completion-sync:path:onchange' "PATH CHANGED"
     # Check if the fpath dirs changed
     local completion_sync_old_fpaths_from_path=( "${(@f)completion_sync_fpaths_from_path}" )
+    # Without this, the comparison below is against an unmodified copy of itself
+    _completion_sync:find_fpaths_from_path

     if [[ "$completion_sync_old_fpaths_from_path" != "$completion_sync_fpaths_from_path" ]]; then
       _completion_sync:debug_log ':completion-sync:path:onchange' "Need to update FPATH from PATH!"
